-- and the pharmacological twin of the dose statement, which is one line and worth having stated. A drug
-- sold as a racemate has one record and two substances in it, and their potencies differ -- for propranolol
-- the (S) enantiomer is about a hundredfold the beta-blocker the (R) is. So no single number stored against
-- the racemate's record is the affinity of both enantiomers, whatever number it is and however it was
-- measured. A record that carries one affinity per identifier therefore carries, for every racemic drug, a
-- number that is the affinity of neither constituent -- and the apparent value a competition assay returns
-- on the mixture is a third number again, lying between them and belonging to the mixture at that
-- composition.
racemate-affinity-not-determined : (v : Nat) → (a : v ≡ 100) × (v ≡ 1) → Empty
racemate-affinity-not-determined v p = transport (λ i → isTrue (eqb 100 ((concat (sym (fst p)) (snd p)) i))) unit
